{"id":"b666228ffebaa5c8","group":"67","path":"67/67-df-interpretation-pullback.md","title":"Pullback Theory under an Interpretation","display":"df-interpretation-pullback — Pullback Theory under an Interpretation","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom","book_abbrev":"67","label":"67-df-interpretation-pullback","aliases":["67-df-interpretation-pullback"],"display":"df-interpretation-pullback — Pullback Theory under an Interpretation","depends_on":["[[67-df-general-relative-interpretation]]"],"source_edition":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition","source_scope":"第 8 章导言，印刷页 119；PDF 第 130 页","verification_status":"source-statement-checked","source_proof_status":"定义与Lemma 1接口已核对；pullback公理集仅保证r.e.，不冒称PR","eligible_as_verified_dependency":true},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Aspects of Incompleteness Lindstrom"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"67"},{"key":"label","html":"67-df-interpretation-pullback"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>67-df-interpretation-pullback</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-interpretation-pullback — Pullback Theory under an Interpretation"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"433a5a5e16d90414\" href=\"?note=433a5a5e16d90414\" title=\"67-df-general-relative-interpretation\">67-df-general-relative-interpretation</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_edition","html":"Cambridge/ASL 2016 reprint of 1997 edition"},{"key":"source_scope","html":"第 8 章导言，印刷页 119；PDF 第 130 页"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-statement-checked"},{"key":"source_proof_status","html":"定义与Lemma 1接口已核对；pullback公理集仅保证r.e.，不冒称PR"},{"key":"eligible_as_verified_dependency","html":"true"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L,K\">\\(L,K\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\">\\(S\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\)</span>、<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t:\\mathrm{Fml}_L\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_K\">\\(t:\\mathrm{Fml}_L\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_K\\)</span> 取 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"433a5a5e16d90414\" href=\"?note=433a5a5e16d90414\" title=\"67-df-general-relative-interpretation\">67-df-general-relative-interpretation</a>，并假设 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{RelInt}_{L,K}(T,t)\">\\(\\mathrm{RelInt}_{L,K}(T,t)\\)</span>。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PB}_{L,K}(t,T)\">\\(\\mathrm{PB}_{L,K}(t,T)\\)</span> 是下式定义的句子公理集，后续用可推导性比较理论，不把公理集相等与定理等价混淆。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PureExt}_K(T,U)\">\\(\\mathrm{PureExt}_K(T,U)\\)</span> 在同一语言 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span> 中定义，允许 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\">\\(U\\)</span> 含不同的等价公理呈示。</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"U\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\">\\(U\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\)</span> 是候选扩张。这里不要求 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S,T,U\">\\(S,T,U\\)</span> 的公理集 PR，也不定义 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PB}\">\\(\\mathrm{PB}\\)</span> 的特定公理表示公式。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{PB}_{L,K}(t,T)&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\{\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_L:T\\vdash t(\\varphi)\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{PureExt}_K(T,U)&amp;\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\\nU\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\land\n\\forall\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\ (T\\vdash\\theta\\Longrightarrow U\\vdash\\theta).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{PB}_{L,K}(t,T)&amp;\\coloneqq\n\\{\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_L:T\\vdash t(\\varphi)\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{PureExt}_K(T,U)&amp;\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\\nU\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\land\n\\forall\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\ (T\\vdash\\theta\\Longrightarrow U\\vdash\\theta).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>书中写 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t^{-1}(T)\">\\(t^{-1}(T)\\)</span>。第119页 Lemma 1 给出 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{PB}(t,T)\\vdash\\varphi\">\\(\\mathrm{PB}(t,T)\\vdash\\varphi\\)</span> 当且仅当 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\vdash t(\\varphi)\">\\(T\\vdash t(\\varphi)\\)</span>；因此若 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> 一致，pullback 也一致，且 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t\">\\(t\\)</span> 是它在 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> 中的忠实解释。证明只用翻译保持逻辑和有限推导，未把这类事实塞作定义。</p>\n<p>若 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\">\\(T\\)</span> 的可推导关系 r.e. 且 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"t\">\\(t\\)</span> PR，则 pullback 的公理集合 r.e.；它通常并非 PR。需要适用第6章 PR 呈示的定理时，应另用 Craig 重公理化，并以定理等价识别所得理论；不能把闭包集合当成既定 PR 公理表。新建前已检索本册所有解释、faithful、local 与 theory-closed 节点，均未定义这个跨语言构造。</p>\n<p>来源：Per Lindström, <em>Aspects of Incompleteness</em>，用户提供 PDF；第 8 章导言，印刷页 119；PDF 第 130 页。</p>\n<p>证明核验范围：定义与Lemma 1接口已核对；pullback公理集仅保证r.e.，不冒称PR。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"67-df-general-relative-interpretation","status":"resolved","id":"433a5a5e16d90414","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[67-df-general-relative-interpretation]]","embed":false},{"target":"67-df-general-relative-interpretation","status":"resolved","id":"433a5a5e16d90414","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$L,K$、$S\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L$、$T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K$、$t:\\mathrm{Fml}_L\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_K$ 取 [[67-df-general-relative-interpretation]]，并假设 $\\mathrm{RelInt}_{L,K}(T,t)$。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"L,K","display":false},{"tex":"S\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_L","display":false},{"tex":"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K","display":false},{"tex":"t:\\mathrm{Fml}_L\\to\\mathrm{Fml}_K","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{RelInt}_{L,K}(T,t)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PB}_{L,K}(t,T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PureExt}_K(T,U)","display":false},{"tex":"K","display":false},{"tex":"U","display":false},{"tex":"U\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K","display":false},{"tex":"S,T,U","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PB}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{PB}_{L,K}(t,T)&\\coloneqq\n\\{\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_L:T\\vdash t(\\varphi)\\},\\\\\n\\mathrm{PureExt}_K(T,U)&\\ \\Longleftrightarrow\\\nU\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\land\n\\forall\\theta\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_K\\ (T\\vdash\\theta\\Longrightarrow U\\vdash\\theta).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"t^{-1}(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{PB}(t,T)\\vdash\\varphi","display":false},{"tex":"T\\vdash t(\\varphi)","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"t","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"T","display":false},{"tex":"t","display":false}],"bytes":2568,"backlinks":[{"id":"fb51163c70a06b3c","anchor":"ref-7","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Int}_{L_A,K}$ 取 [[67-df-general-relative-interpretation]]；$\\mathrm{Con}^K_{T\\upharpoonright_{g_K}k}$ 取 [[67-df-general-consistency]]，是算术句，所以 $t$ 可以应用于它。$\\mathrm{PureExt}_K$ 取 [[67-df-interpretation-pullback]]，$\\mathrm{PRPred}_1$ 取 [[67-df-primitive-recursive]]。"},{"id":"d4e4a9a8f1949a67","anchor":"ref-13","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{RInt}_K(\\mathrm{PA},T,t)$，$P=\\mathrm{PB}_{L_A,K}(t,T)$，取 [[67-df-reflexive-interpretation]]、[[67-df-interpretation-pullback]]。$P$ 以定理闭句子集作为公理集，不假设该集合 PR。"},{"id":"38502195e450dd58","anchor":"ref-72","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../67-df-interpretation-pullback]]"},{"id":"aceae1bb446510ab","anchor":"ref-46","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../67-df-interpretation-pullback]]"},{"id":"161ada0e6be38670","anchor":"ref-63","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../67-df-general-relative-interpretation]]；[[../67-df-general-consistency]]；[[../67-df-interpretation-pullback]]；[[../67-df-reflexive-interpretation]]；[[../67-thm-general-second-incompleteness]]；[[../67-thm-reflexive-interpretation-nonfinite]]；[[../67-lem-general-source-orey-hajek]]；[[../67-thm-reflexive-pullback-equivalence]]；[[../67-lem-general-orey-hajek]]；[[../67-thm-general-orey-compactness]]"}],"outgoing":["433a5a5e16d90414"]}